# MV Daily Shift Report – Automation

> **ALFANAR PROJECTS | O&M – Medium Voltage Distribution Network**  
> Automates daily shift report generation from a Google Sheet → Google Doc.

---

## Architecture

```
Google Sheet (ADF_New_Report)
  ├── Shift_Reports       ← one row per report (Day/Night)
  ├── Shift_Attendance    ← staff per shift
  ├── Fault_Logs          ← faults during shift
  ├── Major_Alarms        ← alarms during shift
  ├── System_Readings     ← incomer & loop readings (every 2h)
  └── Users_Directory     ← staff master list

         ↓  Google Apps Script (Code.gs)

Google Doc (generated copy of template)
  └── Saved to your Drive Output Folder
```

**GitHub** hosts the script code. **GitHub Actions + clasp** pushes any commit on `main` directly to the Apps Script project.

---

## One-Time Setup (≈ 20 min)

### Step 1 – Prepare Google Sheet

1. Open your Google Sheet (`ADF_New_Report`).
2. Note the **Sheet ID** from the URL:  
   `https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/`**`THIS_IS_YOUR_SHEET_ID`**`/edit`
3. Confirm all tab names match exactly:
   - `Shift_Reports`, `Shift_Attendance`, `Fault_Logs`, `Major_Alarms`, `System_Readings`, `Users_Directory`

### Step 2 – Prepare the Google Doc Template

1. Open your Google Doc template (`MV_Daily_Shift_Report_Template`).
2. Note its **Doc ID** from the URL.
3. Verify that the placeholder tags match the format `<<[FieldName]>>` and  
   repeating blocks use `<<Start:[Related TableName]>>` … `<<End>>`.

### Step 3 – Create an Output Folder in Drive

1. Create a new folder in Google Drive (e.g. `MV Shift Reports – Generated`).
2. Note the **Folder ID** from its URL.

### Step 4 – Create the Apps Script Project

1. Go to [script.google.com](https://script.google.com) → **New project**.
2. Rename it to `MV_Daily_Report`.
3. Copy the **Script ID** from: *Project Settings → IDs*.
4. In `apps-script/.clasp.json`, replace `YOUR_APPS_SCRIPT_PROJECT_ID` with this value.
5. In `apps-script/Code.gs`, fill in the three `CONFIG` values:

```javascript
const CONFIG = {
  SHEET_ID:         "YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID_HERE",
  TEMPLATE_DOC_ID:  "YOUR_GOOGLE_DOC_TEMPLATE_ID",
  OUTPUT_FOLDER_ID: "YOUR_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID",
  ...
};
```

### Step 5 – Link GitHub to Apps Script via clasp

Install clasp locally once:

```bash
npm install -g @google/clasp
clasp login       # Opens browser → authorise with your Google account
```

This creates `~/.clasprc.json`. You'll need its contents for the GitHub Secret below.

```bash
# Clone this repo
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/mv-daily-report.git
cd mv-daily-report

# First push
cd apps-script
clasp push
```

### Step 6 – Enable the Custom Menu

1. Open your Google Sheet.
2. You'll see a new **📋 MV Reports** menu (may require a page refresh).
3. Use **MV Reports → Generate Pending Reports** whenever you are ready to generate.

